          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Lorentzian geometry
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime+signature"} spacetime signature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (+,+,+,\ldots,+)
            (which yields
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo-Riemannian metric
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature"} signature
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,+,+,\ldots,+)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+special+relativity"}> theory of special relativity
            ”, and it is
            %em locally
            the context of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+general+relativity"}> theory of general relativity
            ”.
          %p
            Note that while Lorentzian geometry is analogous to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
            (as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
            is analogous to a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian manifold
            is analogous to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            (and insist on
            %strong Minkowski geometry
            for our topic here), but usually one skips all the way to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+geometry"} pseudo-Riemannian geometry
            (which studies
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifolds"} pseudo-Riemannian manifolds
          %h2#lorentzian_cartan_geometry_and_first_order_gravity Lorentzian Cartan geometry and first order gravity
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            by the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifolds"} Lorentzian manifolds
            is to a large extent the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
          %p
            Promoting this perspective from global to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+symmetry"} local symmetry
            yields the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+formulation+of+gravity"} first order formulation of gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            yields
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+cohomology"} Lie n-algebra
            extensions of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            (from the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            in
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
